# .trivyignore — documented suppressions per #82 (tracking) / #83 #84 #87 (children)
#
# Format: one vulnerability ID per line, trailing "#" comments (verified against
# Trivy 0.74.0; the EXPIRY= directive is NOT parsed by this version, so review
# dates are recorded per-entry and enforced via the weekly Container Image Scan
# workflow). Entries are ID-global across all images scanned by trivy-action and
# scripts/scan-images.sh — re-verify at each review date that no *other* image
# relies on these IDs being hidden.
#
# Do not add blanket/untracked entries: every line must cite its tracking issue
# and a review date. See docs/container_security_scan.md.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# osquery/osquery:5.17.0-ubuntu22.04 — #87 (profile: agents, in runtime path)
# Fixes exist in the Ubuntu 22.04 security pocket but the 5.17.0 image series
# has not been rebuilt (verified: newest tag is still 5.17.0-*, 2025-06-27).
# Review by 2027-01-02 (90d). Acceptance: upstream rebuild or 5.18.x.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
CVE-2025-68973  # osquery gpgv 2.2.27-3ubuntu2.3 -> fixed 2.2.27-3ubuntu2.5 upstream; image not rebuilt (#87, review 2027-01-02)
CVE-2026-45447  # osquery libssl3 3.0.2-0ubuntu1.19 -> fixed 3.0.2-0ubuntu1.25 in pocket; image not rebuilt (#87, review 2027-01-02)
CVE-2026-84782  # osquery+dcgm libssl3/libssl3t64 family; fix 3.0.2-0ubuntu1.30 / deb13u3 pending image rebuild (#87, #83, review 2027-01-02)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# nvcr.io/nvidia/k8s/dcgm-exporter:latest — #83 (profile: gpu only)
# Upstream rebuilt (34 HIGH -> 4 findings on 2026-10-04); remainder is the
# Debian 13 OpenSSL family pending NVIDIA's next base refresh.
# Review by 2027-01-02 (90d).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
CVE-2026-75804  # dcgm libssl3t64/openssl-provider-fips; awaiting NVIDIA base rebuild (#83, review 2027-01-02)

